%%{init: {'sequence': {'wrap': true}}}%%
sequenceDiagram
    autonumber
    box Curator side
    participant OFAC as OFAC SDN list<br/>(published file)
    actor Curator as Curator ring authority
    participant CurRing as Curator ring program
    end
    box Shared rails
    participant SPP as SPP<br/>(policy agnostic)
    participant Photon as Photon indexer
    participant Prover as Prover
    end
    box Subscriber side
    participant SubRing as Subscriber ring program
    actor SubOp as Subscriber ring authority
    actor Crazy as Mr. Crazy's wallet
    participant Others as Other subscriber rings
    end

    rect rgba(100, 160, 100, 0.08)
    Note over SubRing, Crazy: baseline, a transfer to a clean recipient
    Crazy->>SubRing: reads the policy config, trusts the rows under the pinned hash, Block resolves to the curator's namespace PDA
    Crazy->>Photon: reads the recipient member's entry, none exists
    Photon-->>Crazy: address non-inclusion proof and both roots
    Crazy->>Prover: one proof over the audit statement, policy_hash, both roots
    Note over Crazy: every live output owner is screened, the sender's change too
    Crazy->>+SubRing: transact(proof, root indices)
    Note over SubRing: reads the pinned policy_hash, resolves the roots by index, verifies one Groth16
    SubRing->>-SPP: CPI ring_transact
    Note over SPP: the instruction carries no member, no list, no answers, the chain cannot tell who was screened
    end

    rect rgba(180, 100, 100, 0.08)
    Note over OFAC, CurRing: the ban, one write
    Note over OFAC: the list names Mr. Evil's address, the curator ingests it off chain
    Curator->>Prover: proves the entry mutation
    Curator->>+CurRing: create_entry(Block, member)<br/>member = hash(confidential view tag)
    Note over CurRing: an ed25519 tag equals the pubkey, a P256 identity hashes its x coordinate, an address ban does not cover it
    CurRing->>-SPP: CPI transact signed by the namespace PDA, carrying its own SPP proof
    Photon->>SPP: polls the chain, indexes the entry
    Note over Photon: a plaintext zero amount UTXO at the claimed address, v0 Active, publicly auditable
    Note over Others: the same entry now governs every subscriber, no further write exists
    Note over SPP: not instant, the forester rolls roots forward and the NULLIFIER_ROOT_WINDOW still admits pre ban proofs
    end

    rect rgba(180, 100, 100, 0.08)
    Note over Crazy: the same transfer, the recipient is Mr. Evil
    Crazy->>Photon: reads the member's entry
    Photon-->>Crazy: live Active Block entry
    alt honest wallet
        Note over Crazy: the witness build refuses with PolicyRuleUnsatisfied before any proof request, nothing reaches the chain, the input UTXO stays unspent
    else patched wallet
        Crazy->>Prover: forged witness
        Note over Prover: unsatisfiable, coverage demands an answer for the instance and no absence branch exists against a live Active entry
    end
    end

    rect rgba(128, 128, 128, 0.07)
    Note over SubRing, SubOp: no local override
    SubOp->>SubRing: create_entry(Block, member) on the subscriber's own ring
    SubRing-->>SubOp: ForeignSource, the list is served by the curator's entries
    end

    rect rgba(100, 160, 100, 0.08)
    Note over Curator, CurRing: the clear
    Curator->>CurRing: update_entry, v1 Cleared at the same address, no delete exists
    Crazy->>Photon: reads the member's entry
    Photon-->>Crazy: cleared entry, inclusion plus nullifier non-inclusion
    Crazy->>SubRing: the same input UTXO lands through the cleared branch
    end

    rect rgba(128, 128, 128, 0.07)
    Note over Curator, SubOp: the real escape is the subscriber's, not the sanctions list's
    Curator->>CurRing: re-bans the member, v2 Active
    SubOp->>SubRing: set_policy_source(Block, own) by the config authority
    Note over SubRing: re-hashes the stored rows over the new map, generation counts one more, the next transfer lands with the curator entry Active
    SubOp->>SubRing: set_policy_rules without the Block rule, by the upgrade authority
    Note over SubRing: the rows and the hash change at once, a proof built against the old table fails verification
    end
